---
import {
  BEAN_INSTITUTE_YIELD_URL,
  DEFAULT_CUPS,
  DEFAULT_DAYS,
  DEFAULT_PEOPLE,
  DEFAULT_PLAN_INPUT,
  UNL_YIELD_URL,
  describeWeek,
  formatMoney,
  householdWeeks,
  priceWeek,
  weekPlan,
} from "../lib/bean-week-math.js";
import { loadBeanWeekPrices } from "../lib/bean-week-prices.js";

const prices = loadBeanWeekPrices();
const initialPlan = priceWeek(weekPlan(DEFAULT_PLAN_INPUT), prices);
const initial = describeWeek(initialPlan, prices);
const households = householdWeeks(prices);
const redCosts = households.map((row) => formatMoney(row.dry.redLentils)).join(", ");
const priceJson = JSON.stringify(prices).replace(/</g, "\\u003c");
const chartAlt =
  "Bar chart of July 2026 dry-bean cost for 2, 4, and 6 people over 7 days at a half cup cooked each. Dry weight is 1.17 lb, 2⅓ lb, and 3½ lb.";
---

<section class="bean-week" data-bean-week-planner aria-labelledby="bean-week-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">Family week planner</p>
  <h2 id="bean-week-heading">Set the people, the days, and the bowl</h2>
  <p>
    The default is {DEFAULT_PEOPLE} people, {DEFAULT_DAYS} days, and a half cup cooked each day.
    Pounds use the
    <a href={BEAN_INSTITUTE_YIELD_URL}>Bean Institute</a>
    and
    <a href={UNL_YIELD_URL}>Nebraska Extension</a>
    yield: 1 pound dry cooks to about 6 cups, and that pound is about 2 cups dry.
    The can count is shown two ways, because the charts don't agree.
  </p>
  <form class="fields">
    <label>
      People
      <input data-input="people" type="number" min="1" max="12" step="1" value={DEFAULT_PEOPLE} inputmode="numeric" />
    </label>
    <label>
      Days
      <input data-input="days" type="number" min="1" max="14" step="1" value={DEFAULT_DAYS} inputmode="numeric" />
    </label>
    <label>
      Cooked cups per person per day
      <input data-input="cups" type="number" min="0.25" max="2" step="0.05" value={DEFAULT_CUPS} inputmode="decimal" />
    </label>
  </form>
  <output aria-live="polite">
    <p data-field="summary">{initial.summary}</p>
    <dl>
      <div><dt>Dry pounds</dt><dd data-field="pounds">{initial.pounds}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Dry cups</dt><dd data-field="dryCups">{initial.dryCups}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Cans at 1 1/2 cups, rounded up</dt><dd data-field="cansKitchen">{initial.cansKitchen}</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Cans at 1 3/4 cups</dt><dd data-field="cansInstitute">{initial.cansInstitute}</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p data-field="cost">{initial.cost}</p>
    <p data-field="canned">{initial.canned}</p>
  </output>
  <p class="note">
    Pinto and black beans are the BLS US average for July 2026. Brown lentils and red lentils are audited Walmart bags in the same study, and those rows don't carry a July date. The one-can swap, including a crowd pot, stays on the
    <a href="/tools/dried-beans-to-canned-converter/">dried beans to canned converter</a>.
    Simmer times for the bag are in
    <a href="/how-to-cook-dried-beans-from-scratch/">how to cook dried beans from scratch</a>.
    A family cart that also has to clear fiber is the
    <a href="/cheapest-family-grocery-basket-for-protein-and-fiber/">cheapest family grocery basket for protein and fiber</a>.
    A week that also holds a batch of chicken or pork is a different clock. Cooked meat and poultry are 3 to 4 fridge days on
    <a href="/how-long-do-cooked-meat-and-poultry-last-in-the-fridge/">how long cooked meat and poultry last</a>.
  </p>
  <noscript>
    <p>The figures above are the default household. They stay on the page if JavaScript is off.</p>
  </noscript>

  <figure class="chart">
    <img
      src="/images/how-many-pounds-of-dried-beans-for-a-week-chart.jpg"
      alt={chartAlt}
      width="1200"
      height="720"
    />
    <figcaption>
      Dry pounds and study cost for 2, 4, and 6 people. Same half cup, same seven days. The table under the chart is the same math, including the penny where black beans and pintos split at six people.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <caption class="sr-only">Seven days at a half cup cooked per person, priced from the July 2026 study packages.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">People</th>
          <th scope="col">Cooked</th>
          <th scope="col">Dry weight</th>
          <th scope="col">Pinto</th>
          <th scope="col">Black beans</th>
          <th scope="col">Brown lentils</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          households.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{row.people}</th>
              <td>{row.cookedLabel}</td>
              <td>{row.poundsLabel}</td>
              <td>{formatMoney(row.dry.pinto)}</td>
              <td>{formatMoney(row.dry.black)}</td>
              <td>{formatMoney(row.dry.brownLentils)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="note">
    Red lentils in that same file cost {redCosts} for those three households. The bag is $1.94 for 16 ounces at Walmart, not the July BLS average. Package prices and weights are in the
    <a href="/data/protein-per-dollar-2026.csv">protein per dollar CSV</a>,
    and the same package prices are in the
    <a href="/data/canned-vs-dry-beans-cost-2026.csv">canned versus dry beans CSV</a>.
    The method is on the
    <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.
  </p>
</section>
<script type="application/json" id="bean-week-prices" set:html={priceJson}></script>
<style>
  .bean-week{margin:0 0 2rem;padding:clamp(1.1rem,3vw,1.75rem);border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-top:4px solid #F29B30;border-radius:1rem;background:var(--card-bg);color:var(--text-color)}
  .eyebrow{font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted-color);margin:0}
  .bean-week h2{font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:750;line-height:1.25;color:var(--heading-color);margin:.5rem 0 .75rem}
  .bean-week p,.bean-week li{line-height:1.6}
  .fields{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;margin:1.25rem 0}
  .bean-week label{flex:1 1 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.5rem;font-size:.875rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--heading-color)}
  .bean-week input{width:100%;min-height:46px;padding:.7rem;border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-radius:.5rem;background:var(--input-bg);color:var(--heading-color);font:inherit;font-size:1rem}
  .bean-week input:focus-visible,.bean-week a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #F29B30;outline-offset:3px}
  .bean-week output{display:block}
  .bean-week output p:first-child{font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;line-height:1.45;color:var(--heading-color);margin:.25rem 0 1rem}
  .bean-week dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:.75rem;margin:0 0 1rem}
  .bean-week dl div{border:1px solid var(--border-color);border-radius:.75rem;padding:.75rem}
  .bean-week dt{font-size:.75rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-color)}
  .bean-week dd{margin:.25rem 0 0;font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:750;color:var(--heading-color)}
  .note{font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted-color)}
  .bean-week a{color:#F29B30;font-weight:650;text-underline-offset:3px}
  .chart{margin:1.5rem 0 1rem}
  .chart img{width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:.75rem;border:1px solid var(--border-color)}
  .chart figcaption{font-size:.875rem;color:var(--muted-color);margin-top:.5rem}
  .table-wrap{overflow-x:auto;margin:1rem 0}
  .bean-week table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.95rem}
  .bean-week caption{caption-side:bottom;text-align:left;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted-color);padding-top:.5rem}
  .bean-week th,.bean-week td{text-align:left;padding:.55rem .4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-color);white-space:nowrap}
  .bean-week thead th{font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-color)}
</style>
<script>
  import { describeWeek, priceWeek, weekPlan } from "../lib/bean-week-math.js";

  function bootPlanner() {
    const root = document.querySelector("[data-bean-week-planner]");
    if (!root || root.dataset.ready) return;
    root.dataset.ready = "true";
    const prices = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("bean-week-prices").textContent);
    const fields = ["summary", "pounds", "dryCups", "cansKitchen", "cansInstitute", "cost", "canned"];
    const nodes = Object.fromEntries(fields.map((key) => [key, root.querySelector(`[data-field="${key}"]`)]));

    function render() {
      const plan = weekPlan({
        people: Number(root.querySelector("[data-input=people]").value),
        days: Number(root.querySelector("[data-input=days]").value),
        cupsPerPersonPerDay: Number(root.querySelector("[data-input=cups]").value),
      });
      const text = describeWeek(priceWeek(plan, prices), prices);
      if (!text) {
        nodes.summary.textContent = "Enter a headcount, a number of days, and a cooked amount above zero.";
        return;
      }
      for (const key of fields) nodes[key].textContent = text[key];
    }

    root.addEventListener("input", render);
  }

  bootPlanner();
  document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", bootPlanner);
</script>
